# Host-name uses that may stay: each records the host and never branches on it.
# Format: path | needle (substring of the line, or * for the whole file) | reason
# Read by bin/lint-host-name; an entry that matches nothing fails the lint.
autodev/bin/alert-lib.sh | host=$(hostname 2>/dev/null | names the sending machine in the Slack alert text
autodev/bin/fleet-digest.sh | HOST=$(hostname 2>/dev/null | records the generating host in the digest JSON (provenance)
slack-ask/SKILL.md | Run `hostname` | names the asking machine in the Slack message
slack-notify/SKILL.md | Run `hostname` | names the sending machine in the Slack message
bin/lint-host-name | * | the lint's own pattern table and docs
bin/test/test_lint_host_name.py | * | fixtures for each refused form
factory-machine/SKILL.md | `socket.gethostname`, `platform.node`, `/etc/hostname` | lists the forms the lint refuses
